# Inertia + React Pages

## Props

- Use props exactly as passed from controllers; do not rename server fields in redesigns.
- Optional chaining for nested data: `stats?.active_exams`, `result.examinee?.full_name`.

## Navigation & forms

```jsx
import { Link, router } from '@inertiajs/react';

<Link href="/guidance/exam-results">View all</Link>

router.post('/guidance/exams', formData, {
  onSuccess: () => setSubmitting(false),
  onError: (errors) => setSubmitting(false),
});
```

## Frontend-only redesign (default for “redesign” requests)

**Read the full page file first** — imports through export — and list every prop and handler before moving UI.

| Allowed | Not allowed |
|---------|-------------|
| Section order, grids, spacing, typography | `*Controller.php`, models, migrations |
| Tabs/collapsibles via `useState` | New Inertia props or renamed server keys |
| Presentational helpers in the same `.jsx` file | New routes or API calls |
| Same `Link` / `router` URLs and form payloads | Deleting empty states or actions |

If data looks wrong, compare with the **original** prop path in the file and sibling pages — do not change the backend unless the user asks.

## Accessibility

- `aria-labelledby` on `<section>` with visible headings.
- Buttons for tabs: `type="button"`, clear active state (e.g. `bg-[#1447E6] text-white`).
- Sufficient contrast on navy/blue backgrounds (`text-white/80` for secondary text).
